cff-version: 1.2.0
message: If you use this benchmark, please cite it.
title: >-
  What a Streaming Decoder Costs: A Five-Gate Benchmark of Twenty Neural Audio
  Decoders, and a Metric That Failed Its Own Validity Check
authors:
  - family-names: Gkilis
    given-names: Panagiotis
    orcid: https://orcid.org/0009-0007-3805-170X
    affiliation: BedVibe Studios
abstract: >-
  Twenty neural audio decoders measured under one frozen five-gate protocol on
  identical audio. Only three of twenty reproduce full-context output from
  partial input with load-bearing state. The sole pre-registered cross-arm
  quality metric failed its own validity instrument: a zero-parameter
  phase-retrieval algorithm scores best on it in six states of six. A second
  measurement sharing no implementation, speaker-embedding retention across
  three separately calibrated encoders, identifies the same three arms as
  losing nothing to streaming. Perceptual quality was not measured.
keywords:
  - neural audio codec
  - speech synthesis
  - streaming audio
  - decoder
  - vocoder
  - speaker identity
  - latency
  - real-time factor
  - audio reconstruction
  - benchmark
